de'i li 06 pi'e 11 pi'e 2008 la'o fy. Luke Bergen .fy. cusku zoi skamyxatra.
> in the word "djica" (desire), how would you pronounce that first part?  I
> can't seem to make the two consonants really separate without inserting an
> "y" type sound between them.  Otherwise it ends up sounding kind of like the
> "dg" in "judge".  Is this ok?
.skamyxatra

"dj" is supposed to be pronounced like an English J (like both the "j" and "dg"
in "judge") as that's what you get when you combine the two sounds.  Similarly,
"tc" is pronounced like English "ch".

